                      (    forth6809.asm):12756         ; ENVIRONMENT? - dispatcher complete; table has entries derived
                      (    forth6809.asm):12757         ; without fabricating unfixed capacities. /HOLD and /PAD were both
                      (    forth6809.asm):12758         ; added this session, answering HOLDMINSIZE and PADMINSIZE
                      (    forth6809.asm):12759         ; respectively (see each entry itself, below, for why each uses its
                      (    forth6809.asm):12760         ; own, conceptually correct constant rather than the numerically-
                      (    forth6809.asm):12761         ; equal PADOFFSET).
                      (    forth6809.asm):12762         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):12763         ; WORDLISTS (16.3.2, Search-Order word set) is deliberately absent
                      (    forth6809.asm):12764         ; from ENVTABLE, not an oversight - this system doesn't implement
                      (    forth6809.asm):12765         ; the Search-Order word set, so WORDLISTS is genuinely an unknown
                      (    forth6809.asm):12766         ; attribute here. Per ENVIRONMENT?'s own spec (6.1.1345): "If the
                      (    forth6809.asm):12767         ; system treats the attribute as unknown, the returned flag is
                      (    forth6809.asm):12768         ; false" - falling through to ENVNOTFOUND already produces exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):12769         ; that, correctly and completely, with no dispatcher work needed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12770         ; Confirmed via MAME testing.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12771         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):12772         ; MAX-D/MAX-UD were resolved this session via a genuine dispatcher
                      (    forth6809.asm):12773         ; extension, not just a table entry - both are double-cell values
                      (    forth6809.asm):12774         ; per their own ANS data type, which the original single-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):12775         ; ENVFOUND (pushing exactly one value before TRUE) couldn't
                      (    forth6809.asm):12776         ; represent. Added a second table (ENVTABLE2) and matching loop
                      (    forth6809.asm):12777         ; (ENV2START/ENV2LOOP/ENV2FOUND, below) specifically for double-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):12778         ; entries, rather than reworking the single-cell path to handle both
                      (    forth6809.asm):12779         ; shapes - see those labels for the full design.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12780         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):12781         ; FLOORED was the third, separate open item flagged previously -
                      (    forth6809.asm):12782         ; investigated this session by tracing DIVCOMMON (shared by /, MOD,
                      (    forth6809.asm):12783         ; /MOD) against this system's own SM/REM and FM/MOD. Confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):12784         ; DIVCOMMON matches SM/REM's convention exactly (remainder sign
                      (    forth6809.asm):12785         ; restored from the dividend's own original sign, not the quotient's)
                      (    forth6809.asm):12786         ; - this system's primary division words use symmetric division, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):12787         ; floored. FLOORED now answers 0 (false) - see the entry itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):12788         ; below, for the full trace.
FCC6 3706             (    forth6809.asm):12789         ENVQUERY: PULU D
